  "definition": "Spacecraft thermal control keeps equipment, structures, fluids and payloads within their survival and operating temperature limits throughout the mission. It manages environmental heat, internally dissipated power, stored energy and radiative rejection. The subsystem commonly combines passive surfaces and heat paths with active heaters, coolers or fluid transport.[^1]",
